<title>HONG KONG: China Overseas Land 1996 net up five pct.</title>
<headline>China Overseas Land 1996 net up five pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	 21.1	  vs 23.4</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)  4.1	   vs 7.1</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	151.87 gain vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			  861.29	vs 820.23</p>
<p>    Turnover		   3,302.11    vs 3,263.86</p>
<p>    Company name	     China Overseas Land &amp; Investment Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		June 12-19</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	 July 8</p>
<p>NOTE - China Overseas Land is a property developer and investor.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain on disposal of investment properties. Share earnings is based on the weighted average of 4.1 billion shares vs 3.5 billion.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is eight H.K. cents (including interim dividend of 3.9 cents) vs 11 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
